Supposé l’incli.n naturelle de 71^{d} 30^{1},
          \begin{array}{c}
            \begin{array}{cc}
            \overbrace{\hphantom{30}}^{b} & \overbrace{\hphantom{73^{d}.50}}^{a}
            \end{array}
            \\
            \left\{
            \begin{array}{c|c}
            30^{d} & 73^{d}.50 \\
            45 & 76.41 \\
            60 & 80.3a
            \end{array}
            \right\}
            \end{array}
          je trouve \[
                \left\{ \;\overset{a}{\ldots}\; \mathrm{pour}\; \overset{b}{\ldots}\; \right\}
                \] de Declinaison.
